GTKHello - riscos-gtk M2 test

A GTK 3 window on the RISC OS desktop, drawn by GTK in the RISCOS theme
through riscos-gtk's RISC OS backend: a label, a "Click me" button, an
"Option" check box and a text entry. The window has normal RISC OS
furniture (title bar, close, back, toggle size, resize).

Try: click the button (the label counts the clicks), click the check box,
click in the entry and type, resize the window by its corner, move it,
close it. Then send back <Wimp$ScrapDir>.GTKHello.Log, a screenshot, and
a note of anything that looked or behaved wrong.

0.4: red and blue no longer swapped on a normal (TBGR) desktop; toggle
size and corner resizing lay the window out at the new size, and the
whole window is painted (no smearing when the big window is moved).

0.3: fixes 0.1/0.2 quitting at once with an empty log (the log was
opened twice; RISC OS allows one write-open per file).

0.2: theme revision 3 (RISC OS 5 sizes and scroll bars); the backend
now gives every GTK program the RISC OS defaults itself (RISCOS theme,
DejaVu Sans 12 for Homerton 12pt, 90 dpi, no animations).

Not done yet: key repeat and Shift/Ctrl combinations beyond the cursor
keys, pop-up menus, the clipboard, drag and drop, pointer shapes.

Needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16+ and ARMEABISupport (PackMan), and a 32bpp
(16 million colour) desktop with RISC OS 5.21 or later (TRGB sprites).

